Korean boy band BigBang. With the release of the group's second studio album Remember (2008), which included a solo performance by Seungri, he began to adopt a more mature image as an artist. Seungri furthered this image with the release of his chart-topping EP, V.V.I.P (2011).","title":"Seungri","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seungri"}},"Q43089418":{"id":"Q43089418","name":"Hui","ko":"후이","birthName":"Lee Hoe-taek","birthNameEn":"Lee Hoe-taek","aliases":["Lee Hoe-taek"],"birth":"1993-08-28","death":"","birthplace":"Gwacheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","songwriter"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"Cube Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q484449","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q29350008","name":"Triple H","start":"2017","end":"2018"},{"id":"Q23936742","name":"Pentagon","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/cube_ptg/","x":"https://x.com/official_HUI","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4R0tSGcVRQ8ZXPzttU8mHy","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/9bb1cdac-5f34-4e9e-8e1c-e9e7b74c83aa"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Lee Hoe-taek, better known as Hui (후이), is a South Korean singer, songwriter and composer. He debuted as the leader, main vocalist and lead dancer of boy group Pentagon in October 2016, under Cube Entertainment. He was a member of the co-ed trio Triple H, alongside former bandmate Dawn and former labelmate Hyuna, and is the leader of trot boy group Super Five of MBC's Favorite Entertainment. He is also well known for his participation in the reality competition series Boys Planet, where he placed 13th overall. Hui participates in writing and producing a majority of Pentagon's songs.","title":"Hui (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hui_%28singer%29"}},"Q493514":{"id":"Q493514","name":"Jihyuk","ko":"지혁","birthName":"송헌용","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1987-07-13","death":"","birthplace":"South Korea","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2007","agencies":[{"name":"Universal Music Group","korean":false,"id":"Q38903","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/xornjsz1/","x":"https://x.com/xornjsz1","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/ad8d8f38-03d8-4b63-b79d-1c99ab53d8d3"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q494154":{"id":"Q494154","name":"Park Bom","ko":"박봄","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Bom"],"birth":"1984-03-24","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2009","agencies":[{"name":"YG Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q50595","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q171885","name":"2NE1","start":"2024","end":"2016"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/newharoobompark/","x":"https://x.com/haroobomkum","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3uHb6dRazmcaT15bMexUtt","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/df8b2247-0ec1-42f6-9a5b-97e0b120ba0d"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Park Bom is a South Korean singer. She is best known as a member of the South Korean girl group 2NE1, which became one of the most popular South Korean girl groups worldwide. Park began her musical career in 2006 under YG Entertainment, featuring on singles released by label-mates Big Bang, Lexy, and Masta Wu. In 2009, she made her debut as the main vocalist of 2NE1. Under YG Entertainment, Park released two solo singles, \"You and I\" (2009) and \"Don't Cry\" (2011), which reached number one on the Gaon Digital Chart, the national music chart of South Korea. She was awarded Best Digital Single at the 2010 Mnet Asian Music Awards.","title":"Park Bom","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Park_Bom"}},"Q55287306":{"id":"Q55287306","name":"Song Yuqi","ko":"우기","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Yuqi","Sòng Yǔqí","Song Yu Qi","Song Yu Ki","Song Yu Gi"],"birth":"1999-09-23","death":"","birthplace":"Beijing","nationality":["People's Republic of China"],"h